# /etc/apt/preferences.d/99-ncz-initramfs-tool
#
# HISTORY, AND WHY THIS FILE NOW SAYS THE OPPOSITE OF WHAT IT USED TO.
#
# This pin previously set dracut to Pin-Priority: -1 to stop apt EVER pulling it
# in, because initramfs-tools was the builder and an `apt remove
# initramfs-tools` would otherwise have been satisfied by silently installing
# dracut and switching builders with no operator decision anywhere.
#
# That gate has now been passed deliberately. dracut is the PRIMARY initramfs
# builder as of 26.7, metal-validated on O6N (Radxa Orion O6N,
# 7.2.0-rc7-sky1-ncz, 2026-08-16): booted to desktop, dracut-112-1 confirmed in
# the journal, zero initramfs-tools fingerprints, root mounted from btrfs
# @rootfs, GPU/VPU/NPU/network/audio all up, zero failed units.
#
# So a negative pin on dracut would now break the shipped configuration. The
# file is kept, empty of pins, as the record of that decision -- deleting it
# outright would leave the next person wondering whether the old pin was lost
# by accident.
#
# WHAT PROTECTS THE BUILDER NOW: linux-image-cixmini depends on
#     dracut | initramfs-tools | linux-initramfs-tool
# with dracut FIRST, so apt prefers it and cannot satisfy the dependency by
# quietly removing it. initramfs-tools is no longer installed in the main image
# at all; it survives where it is actually useful, in the RESCUE partition
# toolkit (manifests/rescue.pkgs), for repairing a target system's initrd.
